  "text": "Recipe: Savory Millet Cupcakes\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Savory Bread\nIngredients: kodo millet, spinach, beetroot, sesame seeds, Amla, Date, mint\nCooking methods: soak, grind, ferment, bake\nInstructions: BATTER: Soak kodo millet overnight. Drain & grind into batter. Let it ferment for several hours (6-7 hours in summers; 10-11 hours when kept in a warm location in winters).\n(1) Pour fermented batter into a cupcake mould. Then add some grated beetroot and spinach as fillings.\n(2) Cover them with another layer of fermented batter.\n(3) Sprinkle some sesame seeds. Bake in air fryer for 25 to 30 mins at 180 C.\n(4) Serve with Mint Chutney & Amia Date Chutney. Upper side is crusty. Inside is soft. Tastes great when freshly made.\n(5) Serve after slicing into halves, showing beetroot & spinach stuffing.\nNotes: Upper side is crusty. Inside is soft. Tastes great when freshly made.",
